candidates.comparison_that_would_overturn:
One collector fan-out run: a single client capture, with the collector exporting traces to Tempo 3.0.3, to ai-observer and to otel-tui. Run one real Claude Code task with tracing on, with ENABLE_BETA_TRACING_DETAILED and every OTEL_LOG_* variable unset. Add a collector drop rule for new_context, system_prompt_preview, user_system_prompt, tool_input and response.model_output, and drop or hash user.email. Measure:
(a) stored span count vs the spans reported in the claude --debug-file log;
(b) zero prompt or tool content in stored spans;
(c) exact prompt.id / session.id joins to Loki events and Prometheus token counters;
(d) RSS and disk on WSL2 and on the 24 GB Mac;
(e) no acknowledged spans lost after kill -9 of the collector (file_storage persistent queue) and of the backend.
Record that direct Anthropic API requests carry a traceparent header when tracing is on. Tempo is overturned if ai-observer or otel-tui answers the same per-task questions with equal completeness at lower footprint, or if Tempo loses spans across a restart.

